                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Can't say I enjoyed this game. It has a great OST, and the fast-paced gameplay really gets your adrenaline pumping. However, I do have a few major complaints:\n\n[b]1. No volume controls:[/b] The OST is great, but it's incredibly loud. Unless you manually adjust the game's volume through your OS's volume mixer, it can be pretty hard on your ears.\n\n[b]2. Too much visual clutter:[/b] When enemies die, they leave behind a lot of smoke that obscures your vision. This becomes especially frustrating when you're getting overwhelmed by enemies and need to see what's happening.\n\n[b]3. Enemies coming from off-screen:[/b] Enemies can move off-screen and reappear from the top or bottom. While this isn't necessarily a bad mechanic, the limited visible area sometimes makes it nearly impossible to react to them in time.\n\n[b]4. No manual control over power-ups:[/b] There's no way to choose when your power-up activates. It would be much better if you could trigger it manually, especially when you're in a tight spot and really need it.",
